# Mysteries of Beadeaux II (jeuno 32): both quests accepted (I's 89, with the Silver Bell): each trade handler answers
# only its own item. A shell: I's tradeMatches fails (nil), II's 92 (the necklace, fame +7 x3); finished: II completed,
# I still accepted. A charm: I's 91 (the rosary); finished: I completed. II set available, then accepted, by a GM; a
# shell: 92 (the necklace already held, fame +7 x3, the shell taken); 92 open with II completed by a GM: no 92 handler
# (no KEYITEM_OBTAINED).
lists LowerJeuno/Sattal-Mansal/onTrigger LowerJeuno/Sattal-Mansal/onTrade LowerJeuno/onEventFinish/89 LowerJeuno/onEventFinish/91 LowerJeuno/onEventFinish/92
char zone=LowerJeuno pos=42.6,3.9,-54 job=WAR lvl=75
keyitem SilverBell
item QuadavCharm
item QuadavAuguryShell x2
login
trigger Sattal-Mansal               # I available: 89 (0)
finish                              # I begun; II added
trade Sattal-Mansal QuadavAuguryShell x1 # I: nil; II: the necklace, fame +7 x3; 92
finish                              # II completed; KEYITEM_OBTAINED
trade Sattal-Mansal QuadavCharm x1  # I: the rosary, fame +7 x3; 91 (II completed: no section)
finish                              # I completed; KEYITEM_OBTAINED
quest Jeuno.MysteriesOfBeadeauxIi available # a GM (accepted over a completed quest would leave it completed)
quest Jeuno.MysteriesOfBeadeauxIi accepted # a GM
trade Sattal-Mansal QuadavAuguryShell x1 # II: the necklace (already held), fame +7 x3; 92
quest Jeuno.MysteriesOfBeadeauxIi completed # a GM, while 92 is open
finish                              # no 92 finish while completed: no message
